From: Airtype downstream
Subject: [PATCH] mtmd: attribute host weights to the registered CPU device

ggml-base's CPU buffer type has a null device pointer. mtmd's weight counter uses that
pointer as its key, so CPU projector estimates include a null device even though their
compute buffers belong to the registered CPU device. The binding rejects the unregistered
entry and the desktop falls back to charging only the projector file, omitting its compute.

Resolve device-less host buffers to the registered CPU device when accounting for weights.
Other unknown devices remain errors, and device-owned buffers retain their original owner.

Observed with llama.cpp b12332 and LFM3-VL-2B's F16 projector on CPU and CUDA 13.3.
Regression coverage: the_projector_is_charged_to_the_device_it_runs_on checks CPU compute
is included and GPU weights stay on the GPU.

Upstream report: not yet filed.

diff --git a/tools/mtmd/mtmd-model.cpp b/tools/mtmd/mtmd-model.cpp
--- a/tools/mtmd/mtmd-model.cpp
+++ b/tools/mtmd/mtmd-model.cpp
@@ -1315,6 +1315,11 @@
     }

     void load_tensors(mtmd_model & model, ggml_backend_buffer_type_t buft, bool no_alloc) {
+        ggml_backend_dev_t weights_device = ggml_backend_buft_get_device(buft);
+        // Host buffers in ggml-base have no owning device; charge their weights to the CPU.
+        if (!weights_device && ggml_backend_buft_is_host(buft)) {
+            weights_device = ggml_backend_dev_by_type(GGML_BACKEND_DEVICE_TYPE_CPU);
+        }
         auto & hparams = model.hparams;
         std::map<std::string, size_t> tensor_offset;
         std::vector<ggml_tensor *> tensors_to_load;
@@ -1364,7 +1369,7 @@
                 loaded_tensor_names.insert(name);
                 cur = data_tensor;
                 // add to weight memory counter
-                model.mem_weights[ggml_backend_buft_get_device(buft)] += ggml_nbytes(cur);
+                model.mem_weights[weights_device] += ggml_nbytes(cur);
             }
             return cur;
         };
